msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Max Auto-tune Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the `max_autotune` parameter in `torch.compile` to automatically select the optimal configuration for Triton kernels.\n"
"\n"
"## Key Points\n"
"\n"
"- `max_autotune` enables the compiler to automatically search for the best-performing kernel configuration\n"
"- This can significantly improve performance but increases compilation time\n"
"- The example compares performance with and without `max_autotune`\n"
"\n"
"## Code Explanation\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch.nn as nn\n"
"from torch._inductor import config\n"
"\n"
"# Define a simple model\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(1024, 1024)\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(1024, 1024)\n"
"        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = self.fc1(x)\n"
"        x = self.relu(x)\n"
"        x = self.fc2(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"# Create model and input\n"
"model = SimpleModel().cuda()\n"
"input_tensor = torch.randn(128, 1024).cuda()\n"
"\n"
"# Compile without max_autotune\n"
"model_no_autotune = torch.compile(model)\n"
"output_no_autotune = model_no_autotune(input_tensor)\n"
"\n"
"# Compile with max_autotune\n"
"model_autotune = torch.compile(model, mode=\"max-autotune\")\n"
"output_autotune = model_autotune(input_tensor)\n"
"\n"
"# Verify outputs match\n"
"assert torch.allclose(output_no_autotune, output_autotune, atol=1e-5)\n"
"\n"
"# Benchmark performance\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"def benchmark(model, input_tensor, iterations=100):\n"
"    # Warmup\n"
"    for _ in range(10):\n"
"        model(input_tensor)\n"
"    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"\n"
"    start_time = time.time()\n"
"    for _ in range(iterations):\n"
"        model(input_tensor)\n"
"    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"\n"
"    return (time.time() - start_time) / iterations\n"
"\n"
"time_no_autotune = benchmark(model_no_autotune, input_tensor)\n"
"time_autotune = benchmark(model_autotune, input_tensor)\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Without max_autotune: {time_no_autotune:.6f} seconds\")\n"
"print(f\"With max_autotune: {time_autotune:.6f} seconds\")\n"
"print(f\"Speedup: {time_no_autotune / time_autotune:.2f}x\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Important Notes\n"
"\n"
"1. `max_autotune` performs extensive search over different tile sizes, block sizes, and other kernel parameters\n"
"2. The compilation time increases significantly with `max_autotune`\n"
"3. The performance benefits are most noticeable for compute-intensive operations\n"
"4. For small models or inference scenarios, the overhead may not be worth it\n"
"\n"
"## Conclusion\n"
"\n"
"`max_autotune` is a powerful feature for optimizing performance-critical models. It automatically finds the best kernel configuration, but requires careful consideration of the trade-off between compilation time and runtime performance.\n"

msgid "max_autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "max_autotune usage example"

msgid "`max_autotune` 是 Triton-Ascend 提供的增强自动调优装饰器，旨在简化多参数调优的代码编写。与社区版 `autotune` 要求用户手动枚举所有 `triton.Config` 不同，`max_autotune` 允许用户仅提供少量基础配置（如分块大小），并自动将相关的编译器选项（如 `num_stages`、`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance` 等）纳入最优组合的搜索空间。用户也可以通过参数列表显式控制搜索范围。"
msgstr "`max_autotune` is an enhanced auto-tuning decorator provided by Triton-Ascend, designed to simplify the code writing for multi-parameter tuning. Unlike the community version of `autotune`, which requires users to manually enumerate all `triton.Config` instances, `max_autotune` allows users to provide only a small set of base configurations (such as block sizes) and automatically incorporates related compiler options (such as `num_stages`, `enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance`, etc.) into the search space for optimal combinations. Users can also explicitly control the search scope through a parameter list."

msgid "**适用场景**：Ascend NPU 上的 `cube`、`mix`、`vector` 算子，尤其适合需要同时调整多个硬件相关参数的场景。"
msgstr "**Applicable Scenarios**: `cube`, `mix`, and `vector` operators on Ascend NPU, particularly suitable for scenarios where multiple hardware-related parameters need to be adjusted simultaneously."

msgid "基本使用示例"
msgstr "Basic usage example"

msgid "以下示例演示了使用 `max_autotune` 对一个简单的向量加法 kernel 进行自动调优。与社区版 `autotune` 相比，`max_autotune` 还会自动将不同的编译器选项纳入调优空间，无需用户手动指定。"
msgstr "The following example demonstrates automatic tuning of a simple vector addition kernel using `max_autotune`. Compared to the community edition `autotune`, `max_autotune` also automatically includes different compiler options in the tuning space, without requiring users to specify them manually."

msgid "import torch\\n"
msgstr "import torch"

msgid "进阶使用：精确控制调优参数"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Precisely Controlling Tuning Parameters"

msgid "用户可以通过 **tuning_params 显式指定需要调优的编译器选项及其取值列表；未指定的参数会使用内置默认值。以下示例展示了如何对多个参数进行组合搜索。"
msgstr "Users can explicitly specify the compiler options to be tuned and their value lists via **tuning_params**; unspecified parameters will use built-in default values. The following example demonstrates how to perform a combined search over multiple parameters."

msgid "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\\n"
msgstr "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune"
